  "note": "Minimal pairs for listening drills, chosen for a Russian-speaking learner specifically. Russian has no phonemic vowel length and no phonemic gemination, so these are contrasts she is effectively deaf to until drilled — a beginner will hear おばさん and おばあさん as the same word. `contrast` says which feature the pair isolates. These are word-level, which is why the kana seed cannot express them: `domain/distractors.py` handles single-syllable confusion, visual and same-row, and neither covers length, gemination or pitch. Intended for `listen_choose`: play one member, show both, ask which was said. `gloss_source`/`gloss_review_status` follow the vocab_lemmas column names in docs/PLAN.md.",
